plaso-bsm.tsv.gz: what plaso's bsm_log parser reads from the two trails in
tests/fixtures/plaso/, written by gen.py from psort's JSON lines output:

  docker run log2timeline/plaso:20260720 log2timeline --parsers bsm_log \
    --storage-file bsm.plaso <the two files>
  docker run log2timeline/plaso:20260720 psort -o json_line -w plaso.jsonl bsm.plaso
  python3 -I gen.py plaso.jsonl | gzip -9n > plaso-bsm.tsv.gz

plaso reads a header's sub-second field as microseconds; OpenBSM writes
milliseconds (bsm_token.c: "We need time in ms"), as praudit shows them.
The field is compared as written.
